==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|mŭlʹ-tĭ-plī'-ər}}, {{IPA|/ˈmʌltɪˌplaɪər/}}, {{SAMPA|/"mVltIplaI@r/}}
** {{a|UK}} {{IPA|[ˈmʌɫ.tɪ.ˌplaɪ.ə(ɹ)]}}, {{SAMPA|["mV5.tI.plaI.@(r\)]}}
** {{a|US}} {{IPA|[ˈmʌɫ.tɪ.ˌplaɪ.ɚ]}}, {{SAMPA|["mV5.tI.plaI.@`]}}
* {{hyphenation|mul|ti|pli|er}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{arithmetic}} A [[number]] by which another (the [[multiplicand]]) is to be multiplied.
#: ''In the expression'' 5 × 7, ''the "5" is a '''multiplier'''.''
#: ''The score '''multiplier''' increases each time you complete a level of the video game.''
# {{context|grammar}} An [[adjective]] indicating the number of times something is to be multiplied.
#: ''English '''multipliers''' include "double" and "triple".''
# {{economics}} A [[ratio]] used to estimate total economic effect for a variety of economic activities.
# {{physics}} Any of several [[device]]s used to enhance a [[signal]]

